        <section class="sec" id="ask">
          <h2>What Should You Ask Any Breeder Before You Pay a Deposit?</h2>
          <p class="opener">Buyers arrive at this question from marketplaces, forums and videos that all raise it and none of them answer it from the breeder's side. Here at C.A.Gs we would rather hand you the questions ourselves, including the ones that are awkward for us.</p>

          <h3>The Five Questions a Real Breeder Welcomes</h3>
          <p>Ask what the health guarantee covers and what voids it. Ask which diseases the bird was screened for and by what method. Ask whether the grey is fully weaned and how old it is. Ask what documentation travels with it. Ask to see the bird live on video today. Five questions, none of them hostile, and together they eliminate almost every fraudulent listing without any expertise on your part.</p>

          <h3>How We Answer Each of Those Five, on the Record</h3>
          <p>Congenital defects and infectious disease, voided by four published exclusions. PBFD, polyomavirus and psittacosis, by PCR. Fully weaned before travel, never earlier, at twelve to sixteen weeks. Five documents in one folder. And yes — name a time and one of us will hold the phone. Those answers do not change depending on who is asking, which is the only real test of whether they are true.</p>
        </section>

